# The door: every operation the Rust core answers (sdk/rust/src/door.rs), once. One line per op:
#
#     name(arg:type, arg:type?, ...) -> result [!]
#
# The five SDKs' thin wrappers are generated from this file (`node tools/gen-door.cjs`; `--check` proves they are current and that
# this list is exactly door.rs's), so an op's name, the order of its arguments, what a missing one means and what comes back are
# stated here and nowhere else. Arguments go to the core by position.
#
# Argument types
#   text      a string                      time     a time (core.md section 3), as text
#   int       a whole number                bool     true or false
#   block     an object that is a block, message or part of one     object   any other object (options, a keypair, a view)
#   blocks    a list of blocks (each SDK takes its own collection and turns it into a list)
#   strings   a list of text                json     any JSON value
#   suite     the name of a suite; missing = the default suite (protocol.json suites.default)
#   arrivals  { hash: time } for a reader that keeps when blocks arrived, else missing
# `unknown_arrival` is text, `inside` or `outside`: what a reader of the recovery reach reads a block whose arrival it does not know as. It is
# required whenever arrivals are given, and there is no default (identity.md, Recovery reach).
# `?` after a type: it may be missing (null). A missing trailing argument is left out of the call.
#
# Result types: text, bool, int, block, blocks, object, strings, refusals ([{ code, detail }]), json; `?` after one: it may be null.
# `!` after the result: the call may fail as a normal answer (a refusal, a bad key or a signature that does not open): the SDK
# hands the failure to its caller. Without `!` a failure is a bug or a wrong argument type, which stops the call.
#
# A block may also be given whole as the first argument of canonical, hash, check and refusals (door.rs `Args::block`).
#
# Core
version() -> text
peers() -> strings
canonical(type:text, state:json, refs:json) -> text !
canonical_json(value:json) -> text !
cbor_encode(block:block, short:bool?) -> text !
